---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ReportError from '../components/ReportError.astro';
import { pageSchema } from '../utils/page-schema.mjs';

// CREATOR CASE KITS — offer page (Lane C, Creator Desk C2, 2026-10-21).
// 2026-10-28: buying OPEN for one kit — the Alexander brothers kit v1.2 is
// Live on Beehiiv at /products/alexander-brothers-creator-case-kit (the v1.1
// product is archived; never link its old slug). The founding plan is still
// "coming soon". No Offer schema yet, so structured data makes no price claim.
// C2b (2026-10-22): cold-eyes fixes 1, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 11, 12 applied.
// Doctrine v2.1 §10: never tell a buyer what they may or may not say; never
// promise updated files. Never print internal file names in public copy.

const TITLE = 'Court Case Kits for Creators';
const DESCRIPTION = 'Sourced court case kits for true-crime YouTubers, TikTokers and podcasters. Status, dates, timeline and sources in one file. Free sample inside.';
const SAMPLE = '/creators/samples/faith-hedgepeth-case-kit.html';
const CONTACT = 'mailto:cassiancreed@cassiancreed.com?subject=' + encodeURIComponent('Creator case kits');
const KIT_KEY = 'alexander-brothers-creator-case-kit';
const kitUrl = (placement) => 'https://cassiancreed.beehiiv.com/products/' + KIT_KEY + '?' + new URLSearchParams({
  utm_source: 'cassiancreed.com',
  utm_medium: 'creators_page',
  utm_campaign: 'creator_kit_alexander_v12',
  utm_content: placement,
});

const jsonld = pageSchema({
  type: 'WebPage',
  title: TITLE,
  headline: TITLE,
  description: DESCRIPTION,
  path: '/creators/',
  source: 'src/pages/creators.astro',
});
---
<Base title={TITLE} description={DESCRIPTION} jsonld={jsonld}>
  <article class="post creators">
    <p class="evidence evidence--accent">For creators</p>
    <h1>Court Case Kits for Creators</h1>
    <p class="post__note">We do the court research. You make the show. Page updated October 28, 2026.</p>

    <div class="quick" aria-label="The offer at a glance">
      <ul>
        <li><strong>What it is:</strong> a PDF research file on one live court case. Every fact links to its source. Our free sample is 6 pages.</li>
        <li><strong>Price:</strong> $29 for one kit, or $39 a month on the founding plan.</li>
        <li><strong>Delivery:</strong> a download link right after checkout.</li>
        <li><strong>Can I buy now?</strong> Yes, for one case. The Alexander brothers kit is on sale now. The founding plan is not open yet.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="quick__actions"><a class="btn" href={kitUrl('creators_quick')} data-book-key={KIT_KEY} data-cta-placement="creators_quick">Buy the Alexander brothers kit, $29</a> <a class="quick__ask" href={SAMPLE}>Read the free sample kit</a> <a class="quick__ask" href={CONTACT}>Ask about a case you cover</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="post__content">
      <h2 id="on-sale-now">Which kit is on sale now?</h2>
      <p>The <strong>Alexander Brothers Case Kit (Creator Edition)</strong>, version 1.2. It is a 13-page PDF for $29. Its facts are as of October 28, 2026.</p>
      <p>It covers the federal case against Alon, Oren and Tal Alexander in New York. A jury found them guilty of sex trafficking and related federal crimes on March 9, 2026. On October 27, 2026, each brother was sentenced to 30 years in prison and 10 years of supervised release, the U.S. Attorney's Office said. They can still appeal. Oren and Alon also face charges in Florida, where they are presumed innocent.</p>
      <p>Inside: a one-minute brief, a map of the key court filings, two timelines, what each side says, and a source for every fact.</p>
      <p><a class="btn" href={kitUrl('creators_on_sale')} data-book-key={KIT_KEY} data-cta-placement="creators_on_sale">Buy the Alexander brothers kit, $29</a></p>

      <h2 id="what-is-a-case-kit">What is a case kit?</h2>
      <p>A case kit is a short research file on one live court case. It is made for people who cover trials on YouTube, TikTok or a podcast. It tells you where the case stands, what happens next, and where each fact comes from. Every fact links to its source. Our free sample is 6 pages long.</p>

      <h2 id="time-saved">How much time can a kit save?</h2>
      <p>Court research takes a lot of time. You have to find the case, check the dates, and sort what each side says from what a court has found.</p>
      <p>A kit does that first pass for you. You still check the newest news before you post. But you start with the case already sorted, instead of 40 open tabs.</p>

      <h2 id="whats-inside">What is inside a kit?</h2>
      <ul class="kit-list">
        <li><strong>Facts-as-of stamp.</strong> The date and time the facts were checked, on page one.</li>
        <li><strong>One-minute brief.</strong> The case in five short lines.</li>
        <li><strong>Status in the record.</strong> Charges, plea, custody, court, judge and stage, each with its source.</li>
        <li><strong>What happens next.</strong> The next court step, its time, and whether that time is confirmed or only reported.</li>
        <li><strong>Timeline.</strong> Dated events from the start of the case to now, each with a source.</li>
        <li><strong>Established, alleged and still open.</strong> What is not in dispute, what prosecutors say, and what is still unknown, kept apart.</li>
        <li><strong>Court rulings so far.</strong> The key rulings and filings, in date order, each with its source. Before a verdict, a plain note says none is a finding of guilt.</li>
        <li><strong>People in the record.</strong> Who is who: the judge, the lawyers and other key people in the record. We never name survivors of sex crimes.</li>
        <li><strong>Name and fact checks.</strong> Spellings that differ between outlets, and dates that conflict, named instead of guessed.</li>
        <li><strong>Key sources and gaps.</strong> A source list, plus a plain list of what we could not verify.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="which-cases">Which cases do kits cover?</h2>
      <p>Kits cover live U.S. criminal cases that we track on our <a href="/court-calendar/">Court Calendar</a>. Our first kits were made for the Faith Hedgepeth, Lindsay Clancy and Lori Vallow Daybell cases. The first kit on sale covers the Alexander brothers case. Want a case you cover? <a href={CONTACT}>Tell us which one</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="free-sample">Can I see a free sample?</h2>
      <p>Yes. Our free sample is the kit for the Faith Hedgepeth case, the 2026 Durham County, North Carolina, murder trial. It is a fixed copy. Its facts are as of October 21, 2026, at 10:52 a.m. Pacific time. At that time the accused man had pleaded not guilty and was presumed innocent, and there was no verdict. Since then, on October 23, 2026, a jury found him guilty; the sample has a dated note at the top that says so. For where the case stands now, see our <a href="/court-calendar/">Court Calendar</a>.</p>
      <p>We do not change the sample's facts, so it shows exactly what a kit looks like on the day it is made. If we find an error, we add a dated correction note. The sample also says plainly what we did not check: for this kit, we did not check the court's own case file (the docket).</p>
      <p><a class="btn" href={SAMPLE}>Read the free Hedgepeth sample kit</a></p>

      <h2 id="each-week">What will members get each week?</h2>
      <p>The founding plan is not open yet. When it opens, members get <strong>Court Week for Creators</strong> every Thursday. Members also get each new case kit we release while they are members.</p>
      <p>Each Court Week sheet lists the coming week's court dates in the cases we follow. For each date it shows:</p>
      <ul class="kit-list">
        <li>the case, the court and the case number when we found one;</li>
        <li>the date and time, marked "confirmed," "tentative" or "time not published";</li>
        <li>where the case stands, in the record's own words;</li>
        <li>what to check before you go live;</li>
        <li>a link to each source, and when we last checked it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="price">How much does it cost?</h2>
      <div class="price-grid">
        <div class="price">
          <p class="price__name">One case kit</p>
          <p class="price__amount">$29</p>
          <p class="price__note">Early price. One kit, one case.</p>
          <p class="price__soon"><a href={kitUrl('creators_price')} data-book-key={KIT_KEY} data-cta-placement="creators_price">Buy the Alexander brothers kit →</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="price">
          <p class="price__name">Founding plan</p>
          <p class="price__amount">$39<span>/month</span></p>
          <p class="price__note">When it opens: Court Week for Creators every Thursday, plus each new kit we release while you are a member.</p>
          <p class="price__soon">Join link: coming soon</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>One kit is on sale now: <a href={kitUrl('creators_price_note')} data-book-key={KIT_KEY} data-cta-placement="creators_price_note">the Alexander brothers kit</a>. The founding plan is not open yet. To see a kit first, read the <a href={SAMPLE}>free sample kit</a>. To ask for a kit on a case you cover, <a href={CONTACT}>email us</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="delivery">How does delivery work?</h2>
      <p>You pay on our newsletter store page. Each kit is a PDF file. After checkout you get a link to download it. Members get each new Court Week sheet and each new kit the same way, as a file to download.</p>

      <h2 id="refunds">What if I need help or want a refund?</h2>
      <p>For a missing download, a refund request, or any other order question, email <a href="mailto:cassiancreed@cassiancreed.com">cassiancreed@cassiancreed.com</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="how-fresh">How fresh are the facts?</h2>
      <p>Every kit shows the exact time its facts were checked. Court cases move fast, and a kit's facts are not changed after that time. If we find an error, we add a dated correction note. For the newest dates, open our free <a href="/court-calendar/">Court Calendar</a> and check its "last updated" time.</p>

      <h2 id="reuse">Can I use the facts in my videos?</h2>
      <p>Yes. You may use the facts and links in a kit in your own work. Please do not resell or repost the kit itself.</p>

      <h2 id="legal-advice">Does a kit tell me what I can say?</h2>
      <p>No. A kit reports what the court record and named news reports say. It is research, not legal advice. The words you use on air are your call. Everyone charged with a crime is presumed innocent unless proved guilty in court.</p>

      <h2 id="who-makes-it">Who makes the kits?</h2>
      <p>Neural Edge Publishing, the team behind this site and its <a href="/court-calendar/">Court Calendar</a>. We build from public records, keep claims apart from proven facts, and put victims first. Read <a href="/about/">how we work</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="report-an-error">Found a mistake?</h2>
      <p>Report an error in any kit or on this page and we will check it against the record. <ReportError pageTitle={TITLE} /></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .creators .kit-list{margin:0 0 18px;padding-left:20px}
  .creators .kit-list li{margin:0 0 8px}
  .creators .post__content a.btn{color:#F6F1EA;background:#A8503A;text-decoration:none}
  .creators .post__content a.btn:hover{color:#F6F1EA}
  .creators .quick{background:var(--bg-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:16px 18px;margin:0 0 22px}
  .creators .quick ul{margin:0 0 12px;padding-left:20px}
  .creators .quick li{margin:0 0 6px}
  .creators .quick__actions{margin:0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 18px;align-items:center}
  .creators .quick a.btn{color:#F6F1EA;background:#A8503A;text-decoration:none}
  .creators .quick a.btn:hover{color:#F6F1EA}
  .creators .quick__ask{color:var(--ink);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
  .price-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin:0 0 18px}
  .price{background:var(--bg-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:18px}
  .price p{margin:0 0 8px}
  .price__name{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3)}
  .price__amount{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:38px;font-weight:600;line-height:1}
  .price__amount span{font-size:17px;font-weight:400}
  .price__soon{font-weight:600;margin-bottom:0}
  @media (max-width:640px){.price-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
